# Where the live products run. Copy to testenv/live.env (git-ignored) in the
# main checkout; every worktree reads that one file. Absent, or
# KNOBAS_LIVE_TARGET=local, they run in this machine's Docker, as always.
# A variable set in the environment wins over this file.
#
# Only KNOBAS_LIVE_*=value lines; the file is read, never sourced.
# testenv/README.md, "Live products on a remote machine (WSL)".

# local | remote
KNOBAS_LIVE_TARGET=remote

# The remote machine's ssh host (an alias in ~/.ssh/config). Its docker
# engine runs the products; one ssh master forwards their ports here.
KNOBAS_LIVE_SSH=knobas-wsl

# Optional. Ports forwarded from this machine's 127.0.0.1 to the remote's.
#KNOBAS_LIVE_TUNNEL_PORTS=3000 3001 3002 3443 3445 8080 8090 8111

# Optional. 1 refuses a second JVM product while one is up (the default for
# local, where the VM has 8 GB); 0 leaves it to the memory budget (the
# default for remote).
#KNOBAS_LIVE_ONE_JVM=0

# Optional, remote only. The products' memory caps may add up to this; past
# it, starting one stops the other JVM product started longest ago. Default:
# the engine's memory less KNOBAS_LIVE_MEM_RESERVE_MB (1536). Each cap is
# KNOBAS_LIVE_{GITEA,TEAMCITY,TEAMCITY_AGENT,JIRA,CONFLUENCE,DB}_MB.
#KNOBAS_LIVE_MEM_BUDGET_MB=8000

# Optional. Jira and Confluence are set up again from empty when their 3-hour
# licence has less than this many seconds left.
#KNOBAS_LIVE_LICENCE_MARGIN_S=3600
